    </div>
    <p class="vb-note"><b>Where it lives:</b> on desktop this panel drops from whichever box summoned it, the hero box or the nav entry, and the `/` key opens it from anywhere; it is the same popover grammar the site's selector-pop already speaks (one open at a time, Esc closes and refocuses, outside click closes). On phone the bottom bar's center slot opens it as a full sheet riding HUKit.sheet with the grabber and hardware-back behavior every other sheet on the site already has. No new interaction grammar anywhere, which is why it will feel native to the site on day one.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- ══ THE BUILD SPEC ══ -->
  <section class="vb-plate">
    <div class="vb-plate-h"><span class="vb-plate-num">S</span><h2>What approving this means</h2><span class="thesis">the build list, in order</span></div>
    <p class="vb-spec">
      <b>1 · Search, first.</b> <span class="lives">Generated index at build time</span> from tools.js + learn/rounds/talk collections + atlas nodes; one search component with keyboard entry; the dead SEARCH_DATA array dies. Search ships BEFORE the new layout so the box on the new door is real on day one.<br>
      <b>2 · The new home page.</b> This comp, in production form: hero at rest is CLEAN ground with the CURRENT canvas compass rose (the one on today's main page, not a stand-in) and a tap hint; the first tap draws the existing hex grid and routes into the hero zone, every further tap rerolls, the 8-tap secret is untouched, reduced motion reveals without animation, and no canvas work runs on load. Nav wordmark carries the existing brand HEX icon (the shipped hu-logo SVGs), not a plain mark. T2 catalog tabs fed from tools.js cluster fields, "New on the site" fed from real dates, doors row, M2 mission block. <span class="dies">Dies:</span> 88vh hero, carousel, trivia stats bar, citations strip, duplicate about mass. <span class="lives">Survives:</span> rose + secret + the whole canvas world (now earned by a tap), live counts, role doors, status pulse.<br>
      <b>3 · Phone chrome.</b> The bottom bar (Home · Tools · Search · Learn · More) on phone widths, replacing the hamburger on the home page first; if it QAs well it extends site-wide in the hub rollout.<br>
      <b>4 · tools.js grows a cluster field.</b> careers-pay / maps-systems / learn-play on each entry, one place, feeding tabs, the tools hub, and search facets alike.<br>
      <b>5 · Measurement.</b> GoatCounter events on search use and tool entry from home, so the test-user round reads on real signals.<br>
      Card thumbnails ship as authored screenshots of each tool (your screenshots-overwrite-same-filename pattern from the OG cards). Elevation vocabulary from this comp (floating search, card lift) gets written into DESIGN.md as the hub-surface addendum before any code, so the hook enforces the new world instead of fighting it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <p class="vb-lede" style="margin-top:44px">Verdict: approve as the build spec, or name the swaps. After approval the same three-round pattern runs on the Tools hub and Learn hub, both of which inherit this door's grammar: search, clusters, dated freshness, bottom bar.</p>
</div>
